php-geos (1.0.0+git20240129-2~jammy1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Update tests/*.phpt assertions for libgeos 3.14.1 default behavioural
    changes. Six tests (000-005) were previously passing 5/6 against
    libgeos 3.10.2 but failing 4/6 against 3.14.1; they now pass 6/6:
    - 001 Geometry: WKT writer canonicalises -0 -> 0; empty intersection
      returns input-type EMPTY (POINT EMPTY rather than GEOMETRYCOLLECTION
      EMPTY for POINT-POINT etc); polygon ring start vertex normalised to
      lex-smallest; collection member ordering changed; mitre-join
      buffer corner clamping shifted; offsetCurve right-side reversed
      orientation + denser interpolation; MULTIPOINT WKT format now
      `MULTIPOINT ((x y), ...)`; argument-type exception messages broadened
      ("Polygon" -> "Surface", "LineString" -> "Curve" / "SimpleCurve").
      Fixed three pre-existing WKT parse-typo testcases that 3.10's lenient
      parser silently accepted (extra `)` in GEOMETRYCOLLECTION literals).
    - 002 WKTWriter: default trim is now TRUE; setRoundingPrecision(0)
      yields trimmed output; setOutputDimension accepts 4 (XYZM); error
      message text broadened to "must be 2, 3, or 4".
    - 004 WKBWriter: getOutputDimension default is now 4 (XYZM); accepts
      4 as valid; error message broadened.
    - 005 WKBReader: round-trip WKT data updated for new MULTIPOINT format.

 -- Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 16:00:00 +0200

